53
00:03:16,820 --> 00:03:18,640
But that was still kind of new form,

54
00:03:18,780 --> 00:03:20,780
so they were still kind of inching into that field.

55
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:25,000
And now I'm in a role where it's just me for all of it,

56
00:03:25,160 --> 00:03:27,640
for the data modeling side, for the BI work,

57
00:03:27,820 --> 00:03:31,440
for the back-end, you know, Python API scripts

58
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:34,320
to pull data, do the incremental loads.

59
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:38,860
And, you know, I took the job knowing, like, hey, you know,

60
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:42,300
this is a lot to ask of a single senior data engineer.

61
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,780
And so this is an opportunity for me to really, like, show what I can do

62
00:03:46,780 --> 00:03:48,480
and leverage that into, like, hey, you know,

63
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:53,240
this role is really more of a, you know, manager of BI, manager of data.

64
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:56,000
So I came in, I implemented Databricks,

65
00:03:56,560 --> 00:03:59,200
