72
00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:21,780
Especially because it was on Azure and I was used to AWS.

73
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:26,460
Like, yeah, it just, it definitely doubled,

74
00:04:26,940 --> 00:04:31,440
it got tripled by my speed and output over that month.

75
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:34,940
And that was important because, you know,

76
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:37,660
I was pitching this new data tool where they were on Power BI,

77
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:41,500
they were on, like, SQL Server Management Studio and Fivetran,

78
00:04:42,040 --> 00:04:44,660
and I was pitching this on, like, yeah, I can do it cheaper,

79
00:04:45,560 --> 00:04:46,940
but also I can do it better.

80
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:52,060
And it's not going to be, you know, a year-long implementation.

81
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:54,360
I can probably do this in, like, three months.

82
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:55,900
And I got it done in a month.

83
00:04:56,870 --> 00:04:59,410
And so to be able to just hit the grud running

84
00:04:59,410 --> 00:05:02,170
and deliver value immediately was amazing.

85
00:05:02,170 --> 00:05:06,890
And it definitely got me the kind of trust capital

86
00:05:06,890 --> 00:05:10,230
that I needed to continue to grow in the role

87
00:05:10,230 --> 00:05:11,710
and get the autonomy that I needed

88
00:05:11,710 --> 00:05:13,930
