89
00:05:15,340 --> 00:05:18,700
But then Grok Bot came and showed up.

90
00:05:19,920 --> 00:05:22,360
So the pain points that I'd been struggling with up to that point

91
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:27,360
were that I could write Python connectors with Claude

92
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:30,180
and then, you know, I could have it

93
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:33,480
write to, you know, files on my local computer.

94
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:38,160
And so I could basically be hands-off with the connector work,

95
00:05:38,460 --> 00:05:39,960
but I could only really do one at a time.

96
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:42,980
And then, you know, testing it was a matter of, like,

97
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,300
okay, we've committed it, we're pushing it, running it.

98
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:46,400
Okay, that didn't work.

99
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:48,780
Copy and paste the errors back into Claude,

100
00:05:48,940 --> 00:05:51,780
see what's going on, try again, and you'll iterate like that.

101
00:05:51,780 --> 00:05:54,120
But still iterate faster than I would have

102
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:56,060
writing a connector on my own,

103
00:05:56,220 --> 00:05:58,460
where a connector might have taken me a day before,

104
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:02,360
you know, if it was a decent API, you know,

105
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:02,980
which always was.

106
00:06:03,480 --> 00:06:07,240
Anyway, the, I was limited, right? It was Claude.

107
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:09,000
