247
00:11:59,140 --> 00:12:02,740
that we had landed on for the code base in it.

248
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:04,700
It took a minute to train up the architect bot,

249
00:12:04,700 --> 00:12:08,240
but I will say, as far as learnings for Grok Bot,

250
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:11,100
having an architect bot and a PM bot,

251
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,740
and this is going to come as no surprise

252
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:14,840
to anybody who has done software engineering

253
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:19,420
in any, you know, to any degree up to this point.

254
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:22,640
Having a distinct architect bot and a PM bot

255
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:24,500
has been a game changer,

256
00:12:24,600 --> 00:12:26,060
and spending the time to get those right

257
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:27,900
has been a game changer for actually, like,

258
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:29,860
getting work done and doing it in a way

259
00:12:29,860 --> 00:12:30,480
where I'm not, like,

260
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,800
having to constantly go back and manage tech debt

261
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:35,960
and handle things that are, you know,

262
00:12:36,280 --> 00:12:38,420
we're making updates and that's breaking other things, you know?

263
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:42,840
So that's one of the main learnings for me so far.

264
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:46,620
Now, where do things go from here?

265
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:50,790
Personally, you know, I try to avoid being, like,

266
00:12:50,910 --> 00:12:53,790
a fanboy of, like, one specific tool,

267
00:12:54,950 --> 00:12:56,170
and, you know, obviously,

268
00:12:56,210 --> 00:12:57,890
