00:12:58,250 --> 00:13:01,230
because people are always pushing out new exciting things,

270
00:13:01,470 --> 00:13:02,270
especially right now,

271
00:13:02,970 --> 00:13:05,550
but the two that I will bet on every time right now

272
00:13:05,550 --> 00:13:08,530
are Databricks, because, you know,

273
00:13:08,590 --> 00:13:09,830
with all the AI, you might think

274
00:13:10,710 --> 00:13:15,130
you don't need a data warehouse anymore,

275
00:13:15,250 --> 00:13:16,270
you don't need a BI tool, like,

276
00:13:16,330 --> 00:13:19,130
because the bots can just do it, right?

277
00:13:19,230 --> 00:13:20,470
They can just tell you what you want to know,

278
00:13:20,650 --> 00:13:21,430
but the problem is,

279
00:13:22,530 --> 00:13:24,450
you have to connect those bots every time

280
00:13:24,450 --> 00:13:27,420
to figure out, you know, those answers,

281
00:13:27,960 --> 00:13:29,480
but then the other thing is

282
00:13:29,980 --> 00:13:32,480
when there are specific definitions at play,

283
00:13:32,540 --> 00:13:34,320
I'm like, this is how we calculate net revenue.

284
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:37,920
We, you know, subtract the landed cost of the good,

285
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:45,170
and then we subtract any refunds and returns in the period

286
00:13:45,170 --> 00:13:46,610
versus, you know, when we look at it

287
00:13:46,610 --> 00:13:47,750
for the lifetime of the product,

288
00:13:47,990 --> 00:13:51,670
we do the returns netted out against the original sale,

289
00:13:51,910 --> 00:13:53,610
and so you have, you know,

290
00:13:53,610 --> 00:13:55,430
numbers that are kind of changing back in time

291
00:13:55,430 --> 00:13:56,890
on returns that are happening now,

292
00:13:57,890 --> 00:13:59,250
and so there's, you know, things like that

293
00:13:59,250 --> 00:14:00,980
that are like definitions,

294
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,520
things that you have coded into a data warehouse

295
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:06,260
that you don't want to have to coach your AIs

296
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:08,360
through every time you do an inquiry,

297
00:14:08,860 --> 00:14:11,620
which kind of gets into this concept of like a company brain,

298
00:14:11,720 --> 00:14:12,840
which is something that I know is,

299
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:15,880
is a topic for people right now,

300
00:14:16,380 --> 00:14:18,860
but, so data warehouse is kind of like

301
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:21,880
step one of the company brain, you know,

302
00:14:22,200 --> 00:14:24,180
something where when you ask this question,

303
00:14:24,560 --> 00:14:26,280
you want to ask it and know that it's going to give you

304
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:27,620
the same answer that it's giving your neighbor,

305
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:29,980
and when you don't have a data warehouse,

306
00:14:30,480 --> 00:14:31,720
you can't be as sure of that,

307
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,020
and so data warehouse is still important,

308
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:35,700
and if you're going to have a data warehouse,

309
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:37,640
I highly, highly recommend Databricks.

310
00:14:38,380 --> 00:14:41,440
It's just really scalable, really flexible.

311
00:14:42,180 --> 00:14:43,700
They're always coming out with new features,

312
00:14:43,700 --> 00:14:45,360
which is probably the biggest thing for me

313
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:47,660
between Databricks and Grok Bot

314
00:14:47,660 --> 00:14:49,600
is just that they're always coming out with new features,

315
00:14:49,700 --> 00:14:50,960
they're always making it more useful,

316
00:14:51,160 --> 00:14:53,300
and the features that they're landing make sense.

317
00:14:54,040 --> 00:14:55,720
It's not just silly, stupid stuff

318
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:59,460
like you see with some of the SaaS stuff going on there,

319
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:02,700
and even, I mean, Databricks itself and Grok Bot,

320
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:05,400
